  "rationale": "The representative prefix ends in the preposition “with,” but the model assigns nearly all probability to the determiner “a” rather than the observed proper name. The batch and replay documents both support person names as continuations of this phrase (“A day with Lily” and “A day with Tom”). Add a bounded suffix rule to each available person-name root, rather than hard-coding a single observed name. This increases probability for the supported class while retaining alternatives. A counterexample is a context where “with” is followed by a common noun or another grammatical continuation; the rule does not make those continuations impossible. This provisional repair has not passed the replay gate.",
